black) plus three accents. Migrated from
the-screen/display/06-screen (Properties in the Mode Line).

** Properties in the Mode Line

Certain text properties are meaningful in the mode line. The face property affects the appearance of text; the help-echo property associates help strings with the text, and keymap can make the text mouse-sensitive.

There are four ways to specify text properties for text in the mode line:

Put a string with a text property directly into the mode line data structure, but see The Data Structure of the Mode Line for caveats for that.
Put a text property on a mode line %-construct such as ‘%12b’; then the expansion of the %-construct will have that same text property.
Use a (:propertize elt props…) construct to give elt a text property specified by props.
Use a list containing :eval form in the mode line data structure, and make form evaluate to a string that has a text property.
You can use the keymap property to specify a keymap. This keymap only takes real effect for mouse clicks; binding character keys and function keys to it has no effect, since it is impossible to move point into the mode line.

When the mode line refers to a variable which does not have a non-nil risky-local-variable property, any text properties given or specified within that variable’s values are ignored. This is because such properties could otherwise specify functions to be called, and those functions could come from file local variables.

** Accent faces
Three accents on the mono base, nothing more. Keyboard letters use
bold default (loud by position, first on the line, needs no color).
#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defface manifolding-modeline-modified-face
  '((t :inherit mode-line :foreground "#FFB454"))
  "Dirty/read-only letter. Amber, subtle on the mono base.")

(defface manifolding-modeline-error-face
  '((t :inherit mode-line :foreground "#FF6B6B" :weight bold))
  "Errors. Red, the loudest thing on the bar.")

(defface manifolding-modeline-ok-face
  '((t :inherit mode-line :foreground "#7EC8A9"))
  "Clean/ok states. Quiet green.")

(defface manifolding-modeline-keyboard-face
  '((t :inherit mode-line :weight bold))
  "Keyboard state letters. First on the line, bold default.")

(defface manifolding-modeline-info-face
  '((t :inherit mode-line :foreground "#9AA5B1"))
  "Neutral info (atlas context in the optional header row).")
#+end_src
